{"step_index":269,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:14:18Z","thinking":"**Confirming Build Success**\n\nI've just confirmed the backend build is fully successful, and all nine unit tests have passed. That included the ComplexityEstimator, EfficiencyEngine, and EloRatingService tests. Now I'm shifting focus to constructing the frontend components, starting with the Navbar.\n\n\n**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nI'm now deep into designing the frontend. Specifically, I'm focusing on the component breakdown. So far, the Navbar's looking good with the \"CodeDuel\" neon badge, links, and user status display. Next up is the Footer, which will display the system status and quick links. I've also outlined the structure for a flashy countdown overlay. I'm especially excited about the OpponentCard, which will feature live telemetry and test progress. Finally, I'm working on the ServerTimer and a language selector for the code editor.\n\n\n**Defining Code Editor Elements**\n\nI'm currently fleshing out the core code editor components. Specifically, I'm focusing on the code editor itself, and what should be included. This is shaping up as a crucial element. The editor will have an auto-save function with draft recovery, reset code, run code, and submit solution buttons with loading states.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';\\nimport { Link, useNavigate, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';\\nimport { useAuth } from '../context/AuthContext';\\nimport { useWebSocket } from '../context/WebSocketContext';\\nimport { notificationApi } from '../api';\\nimport { Swords, Code2, Trophy, History, LayoutDashboard, Bell, Shield, LogOut, User as UserIcon, Sparkles } from 'lucide-react';\\n\\nexport const Navbar = () => {\\n  const { user, isAuthenticated, logout } = useAuth();\\n  const { connected } = useWebSocket();\\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\\n  const location = useLocation();\\n\\n  const [notifications, setNotifications] = useState([]);\\n  const [unreadCount, setUnreadCount] = useState(0);\\n  const [showNotifs, setShowNotifs] = useState(false);\\n  const [showProfileMenu, setShowProfileMenu] = useState(false);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (isAuthenticated) {\\n      loadNotifications();\\n    }\\n  }, [isAuthenticated]);\\n\\n  const loadNotifications = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      const res = await notificationApi.getNotifications(10);\\n      if (res.data) {\\n        setNotifications(res.data);\\n        setUnreadCount(res.data.filter(n => !n.isRead).length);\\n      }\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.debug('Failed to fetch notifications:', err);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleMarkAllRead = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      await notificationApi.markAllAsRead();\\n      setUnreadCount(0);\\n      setNotifications(prev => prev.map(n => ({ ...n, isRead: true })));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(err);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const navLinks = [\\n    { name: 'Dashboard', path: '/dashboard', icon: LayoutDashboard },\\n    { name: 'Versus (1v1)', path: '/versus', icon: Swords, highlight: true },\\n    { name: 'Practice', path: '/practice', icon: Code2 },\\n    { name: 'Leaderboard', path: '/leaderboard', icon: Trophy },\\n    { name: 'Matches', path: '/matches', icon: History },\\n  ];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <nav className=\\\"sticky top-0 z-40 bg-dark-900/90 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-dark-700\\\">\\n  \n<truncated 9328 bytes>","Description":"\"Navbar component with real-time status and profile menu\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\codeduel\\\\frontend\\\\src\\\\components\\\\Navbar.jsx\"","toolAction":"\"Creating Navbar.jsx\"","toolSummary":"\"Write Navbar component\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
