{"step_index":277,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:14:40Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 1 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. I want you to build a complete production-oriented full-stack application called **CodeDuel** — a real-time **1v1 competitive programming platform** inspired by modern coding-platform Versus experiences.\r\n\r\nThe platform should allow two users to compete against each other on the same programming problem in real time.\r\n\r\nThe core experience should be:\r\n\r\n**Find Opponent → Match Found → Countdown → Same Problem → Code → Submit → Judge → Compare Performance → Winner → Rating Update → Match Analysis**\r\n\r\nThe application must feel like a real competitive product, not a basic CRUD project.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 1. TECHNOLOGY STACK\r\n\r\n## Frontend\r\n\r\nUse:\r\n\r\n* React.js\r\n* JavaScript or TypeScript\r\n* React Router\r\n* Tailwind CSS or clean CSS\r\n* Monaco Editor\r\n* Axios\r\n* WebSocket/STOMP client if appropriate\r\n\r\n## Backend\r\n\r\nUse:\r\n\r\n* Java\r\n* Spring Boot\r\n* Spring Security\r\n* Spring Data JPA\r\n* REST APIs\r\n* WebSockets\r\n* JWT authentication\r\n* BCrypt\r\n\r\n## Database\r\n\r\nUse:\r\n\r\n* MySQL\r\n\r\n## Real-Time / Per\n<truncated 35551 bytes>\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n- **Build complete full-stack CodeDuel platform (1v1 competitive programming platform)**:\n  - **Status**: IMPLEMENTATION (Phase 3: Frontend components & pages creation and verification)\n  - **Core Flow**: Find Opponent → Redis Matchmaking (expanding window $\\pm 50 \\to \\pm 100 \\to \\pm 200$) → Match Created → 3... 2... 1... Countdown → Same Problem → Code in Monaco Editor → Submit → Isolated Judge Sandbox → Compare Correctness + Normalized Efficiency (70% Runtime + 30% Memory) + Speed → Winner Determination → Elo Rating Update → VS Result Screen & Post-Match Deep Analysis.\n  - **1,000-Problem Curated Que\n<truncated 9856 bytes>\n (Side-by-side performance radar/charts, runtime/memory percentiles, optimization hints).\n2. **Pages**:\n   - `frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx`\n   - `frontend/src/pages/Login.jsx` & `Register.jsx`\n   - `frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx` (Player rating card, quick actions, recent duels, recommendations)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/MatchmakingLobby.jsx` (`/versus` radar animation, filter selector, cancel button)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/VersusArena.jsx` (`/versus/:matchId` 3-column live competitive battle layout)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/PracticeList.jsx` (1,000 problem browser with filters, search, pagination)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/PracticeWorkspace.jsx` (`/practice/:problemId` standalone solver)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/Leaderboard.jsx` (Global top rankings)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/MatchHistory.jsx` (Match log & analysis modal)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/ProfileAnalytics.jsx` (Rating graph, topic mastery radar, stats, achievements)\n   - `frontend/src/pages/AdminDashboard.jsx` (Question bank CRUD, stats, moderation)\n3. **App Routing & Root**:\n   - `frontend/src/App.jsx` and `frontend/src/main.jsx`\n4. **Docker & Deployment**:\n   - `docker-compose.yml` and `.env.example`\n5. **Verification**:\n   - Run `npm install` and `npm run build` in `frontend/` to confirm zero build errors.\n   - Run a test script / verification simulation.\n\nYou have the 1 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f668fdc3-2f5e-43c4-b0e4-81b7b8801342/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T20:05:58Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\rajan\